Separate browser movie video deadlines from audio output progress.

Wine MCIAVI_player schedules pictures with currenttime_us/QPC independently
of its WaveOut clock. Production Chromium previously froze picture 26 across
754 ms of declared AudioContext suspension, while the independent performance
clock advanced. Wine's player reads QPC directly for its frame deadlines.
Use the performance clock for video after playback begins; retain the existing
output timestamp contract solely for source-consumption completion. Browser
initial autoplay suspension still defers the initial video epoch until normal
activation, and later audio suspension does not pause that epoch. Preserve all
source PCM, frame deadlines, reset order and independent drain timers.

--- a/dd2_movie_platform.c
+++ b/dd2_movie_platform.c
@@ -39,6 +39,18 @@
         return outputTime;
     };
     source.onended=function(){Module._dd2movieDone=true;};
+    /* Defer the initial video epoch only while browser autoplay waits for
+       activation. After starting, video follows the independent performance
+       clock even if the audio device later stalls or is suspended. */
+    var videoHeld=ac.state==='running' ? null : performance.now(),videoOffset=0;
+    Module._dd2movieVideoTime=function(){
+        var now=performance.now();
+        if(videoHeld!==null){
+            if(ac.state!=='running')return videoHeld;
+            videoOffset=now-videoHeld;videoHeld=null;
+        }
+        return now-videoOffset;
+    };
